A helicopter crash in Malaysia killed six people, including the country's former ambassador to the US and a high-ranking PM staff member. Prime Minister Najib ordered an investigation and praised the victims as dedicated public servants. The helicopter's flight recorder was found in good condition, and a preliminary report is expected within a week."}
